<document xmlns="urn:hl7-org:v3" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <id root="sample-doc-id-001"/>
  <code code="34391-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="HUMAN PRESCRIPTION DRUG LABEL"/>
  <title>LIPITOR (atorvastatin calcium) tablet, film coated</title>
  <effectiveTime value="20240115"/>
  <setId root="sample-setid-complete-001"/>
  <versionNumber value="1"/>
  <author>
    <assignedEntity>
      <representedOrganization>
        <name>Pfizer Laboratories Div Pfizer Inc</name>
      </representedOrganization>
    </assignedEntity>
  </author>
  <component>
    <structuredBody>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34088-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="BOXED WARNING SECTION"/>
          <title>WARNING: RISK OF SEVERE ADVERSE REACTIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>LIPITOR should be discontinued if markedly elevated CK levels occur or myopathy is diagnosed or suspected.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34067-9" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="INDICATIONS &amp; USAGE SECTION"/>
          <title>1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>LIPITOR is an HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor indicated as an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, apo B, and TG levels.</paragraph>
            <list>
              <item>Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults</item>
              <item>Hyperlipidemia and Mixed Dyslipidemia</item>
            </list>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34070-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="CONTRAINDICATIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>4 CONTRAINDICATIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>LIPITOR is contraindicated in patients with acute liver failure or decompensated cirrhosis.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="43685-7" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>5 WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>General warnings concerning statin therapy.</paragraph>
          </text>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="SPL UNCLASSIFIED SECTION"/>
              <title>5.1 Myopathy and Rhabdomyolysis</title>
              <text>
                <paragraph>LIPITOR may cause myopathy (muscle pain, tenderness, or weakness with elevated CK) and rhabdomyolysis.</paragraph>
                <paragraph>Rare fatalities have occurred as a result of rhabdomyolysis in patients treated with statins.</paragraph>
              </text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="SPL UNCLASSIFIED SECTION"/>
              <title>5.2 Immune-Mediated Necrotizing Myopathy</title>
              <text>
                <paragraph>There have been rare reports of immune-mediated necrotizing myopathy (IMNM), an autoimmune myopathy.</paragraph>
              </text>
            </section>
          </component>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34084-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="ADVERSE REACTIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>6 ADVERSE REACTIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>The following serious adverse reactions are discussed in greater detail in other sections of the label:</paragraph>
          </text>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="SPL UNCLASSIFIED SECTION"/>
              <title>6.1 Clinical Trials Experience</title>
              <text>
                <paragraph>Most common adverse reactions (incidence &gt;= 2%) in patients were nasopharyngitis, arthralgia, diarrhea, pain in extremity, and urinary tract infection.</paragraph>
              </text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="SPL UNCLASSIFIED SECTION"/>
              <title>6.2 Postmarketing Experience</title>
              <text>
                <paragraph>The following adverse reactions have been identified during post-approval use: thrombocytopenia, allergic reactions, hepatic failure, rhabdomyolysis.</paragraph>
              </text>
            </section>
          </component>
        </section>
      </component>
    </structuredBody>
  </component>
